TensorFold dsv41: the RDMA ring opens the GID index TF_RDMA_GID_INDEX names

The two-node line (deepseek-v41-zig-tp2) opens GID index 5 of each RDMA
device and reads no setting for it (the recipe's RUNNING.md, section 2). A
link whose RoCE v2 address sits at another index (index 3 on the lab's DGX
Sparks, where index 5 does not exist) cannot run it. Both ring openings in
model.zig now take the index from TF_RDMA_GID_INDEX: 5 when it is unset, as
before; a whole number from 0 to 255 otherwise, anything else stopping the
start. The node sets it, and NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX, from the link's declared
gid_index (node/tensorfold.hl `lanes_env`).

